    "created_at": "2025-02-17T14:18:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-17T14:18:26Z",
    "body": "That seems like quite a shortcut. `putImageData` *is* special. It anecdoctically also isn't affected by shadows or global alpha, but more importantly, it does bypass the clipping region and will bypass the layers. This isn't something one can do with `drawImage()`.\n\nRegarding the premult and color conversion, it might indeed need to be in the normative texts and not just in the note below.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
